kubeos-dashboard (0.1.0-1kubeos2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild with the plugin published as id "kubeos" again. The 1kubeos1 package
    shipped it as "kubeos-branding": Headlamp enables plugins per id, so a browser
    that had enabled the KubeOS plugin in an earlier install stopped loading it and
    the KubeOS pages disappeared on a freshly installed node. Code unchanged.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:20:00 +0530

kubeos-dashboard (0.1.0-1kubeos1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging. The release archive is built from this repository with
    deploy/binary/build-binary.sh (offline, from vendor/) at package build time, and
    installed at /usr/share/kubeos/dashboard/ with the RELEASE marker and SHA256 that
    kubeos-dashboard-install expects, so the first-boot installer is untouched.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:15:00 +0530
